 "content_notes": "Tone: gross-funny, never gory. The dead rats are a stylised, non-graphic drawing: grey fur, a stitched seam, no blood, no wound, no insides shown; the seized items are drawn as generic phones, chargers and plain packets beside the rat. The throwers were never identified: anonymous dark silhouettes only. The officers and the young man with the drone are generic figures, never named; no badge, crest or insignia of any real prison service; no inmate is shown or mocked. The prison is a generic illustration, not a replica of HMP Guys Marsh. Every card is our own typed graphic; no real photograph is imitated. No dialogue is invented. The teddy-bear comparison is the narrator's joke, not a source's. Status verified 2026-10-17.",
